// Two modules each declare `enum Color`. Each uses its own correctly on the
// interpreter. Enum types are identified by name alone, so analysis cannot tell
// the two apart, and a value of one passed to the other matched by variant name
// on the interpreter but by tag on the JIT — silently different answers. Until
// enum types carry their declaration's identity, the JIT refuses any program
// in which two modules declare the same enum name (SKIP), even this one, where
// values never cross.
#![imports]
a: use "./t_import_enum_same_name_a_lib"
b: use "./t_import_enum_same_name_b_lib"

print(a.code(a.red()))
print(b.code(b.red()))
